Package: uuway
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: GaryOAO <62834599+GaryOAO@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-dbus, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-atspi-2.0, xvfb, xclip, procps, libgtk-3-bin, udev, systemd@SHLIBS@
Recommends: fcitx5
Suggests: winehq-stable (>= 11.0)
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/GaryOAO/UUWay
Description: NetEase UU Remote host for Linux, with native Wayland capture and NVENC
 UUWay runs the official UU Remote Windows host under Wine and hands every
 Windows interface it relies on to a native Linux implementation: GPU
 zero-copy screen capture through the Wayland/PipeWire portal, NVENC hardware
 encoding, uinput keyboard and mouse, Fcitx5 text input, clipboard, file
 transfer, and a Linux login shell as the remote terminal.
 .
 UU Remote itself is not included. Run "uuway setup" as your normal user to
 install it from the official Windows installer into a private Wine prefix.
 .
 Requires GNOME on Wayland, an NVIDIA GPU with NVENC and the proprietary
 driver, and WineHQ stable 11.0 (not packaged by Ubuntu; "uuway setup --system"
 adds the WineHQ repository).
